\par\par \b \uc2  HK dollar brushes against key support at HK$7.75. \b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, April 3 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar brushed against the key support level of 7.75 per U.S. dollar in early Friday trade, a level that dealers say would trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA). \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is stable and we do not comment on money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a spokeswomen at the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  "At least one \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deal was transacted at HK$7.75 per U.S. dollar, but there is no major break below that level" a senior dealer at a major bank said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7498/01 per U.S. dollar at 0230 GMT, slightly weaker than HK$7.7493/03 at the open and HK$7.7490/00 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  The three-month rose by at least 50 points to 270-300 points at 0225 GMT versus 220-270 at the open and 230-260 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  The six-month was up at 880-930 points versus 750-800 points at the open and 775-830 at the close. \par \par \uc2  "The local money market was becoming uneasy as the Japanese yen broke its key support at 134 per U.S. dollar, but market participants were less panicky than they were last October," another senior dealer at a note-issuing bank said. \par \par \uc2  "There is no major selling of the Hong Kong dollar spot," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that while they saw bids on forwards rising, as more participants took a short position against the Hong Kong dollar on fear of a spillover effect from the yen, the upside on dollar forwards would be capped by increasing offers on profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  "Many players who had gone long in forwards a few weeks ago, as forwards rates plunged to pre-Asian crisis levels, are looking for an opportunity to cover their positions," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Frederic Laine, head of interest rate and derivative trading at Credit Lyonnais, said he believed forwards would be range-bound and he did not see any major selling on the Hong Kong dollar spot. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they heard that more than one note-issuing bank was on the bid side of the Hong Kong dollar spot and was believed to be acting on behalf of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to cap the strength of the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Local term money rates were moderately firmer across the board partly on routine demand ahead of a long weekend. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong financial markets will be closed on April 6 for a public holiday and will reopen from April 7-9 before closing again on April 10 and 13 for the Easter holidays. \par \par \uc2  "Interbank liqudity was tighter than yesterday but still abundant especially at the short end," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates remained below five percent, quoted at 4.43-4.93 percent versus 4.68-4.75 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  The one-month was moderately firmer at 5.87-6.0 versus 5.46-5.60 at the close. \par \par \uc2  The three-month was higher at 7.18-7.37 versus 6.75-7.00 at the close. The six-month was firmer at 7.75-8.12 versus 7.50-7.75 at the close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were waiting for Europe and New York to start trading later on Friday for clues on market direction. \par \par \uc2  "Forward rates could firm up once London starts trading, as overseas traders tend to have a bearish view on the Hong Kong dollar," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But they said banks in Hong Kong were increasingly cautious about lending large amounts of Hong Kong dollars to speculators to fund positions on fears of being penalised by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The HKMA said in October it would levy penal rates on banks that repeatedly borrowed from its Liquidity Adjustment Facility (LAF) or discount window on views that these funds would be used to fund speculative attacks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - Angi Li 852-2847-4039; Fax 852-2845-0636. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du43080sk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
