\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor Rises On Fear Of Tightened Fund Supplies \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1998\par 11:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates rose by as much as one percentage point late Friday amid fears that regional instability would again lead to interest rates spikes. \par \par \uc2  While interest rates on the shorter term funds was still soft, long-term rates have shot up as banks scrambled to lock in funds in case the regional situation deteriorated over the long weekend. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate was quoted at 4.50% after hitting a high of 5.0% in the morning, up from 4.25% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month rate was at 7.625%, up from 6.625% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The six-month rate also moved up to 8.25%, up from 7.625% the previous session. \par \par \uc2  At 0910 GMT (4:10 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7483, stronger than HK$7.7496 late Thursday after reports that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in early Friday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said banks were wary of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  edging too close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trigger point. \par \par \uc2  They were worried that any heavy-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might lead to spikes in interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  'Coupled with that, banks tend to be more cautious ahead of a long weekend. So they would cover any short positions or borrow more, just to be on the safe side,' said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The weak Japanese yen and the announcement by Moody's Investors Service to downgrade Japan's outlook to negative from stable generated an atmosphere of nervousness throughout the day's trading. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates surged to almost 50% in late October after a speculative assault on the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  In the futures market, the three-month June Hibor futures contract was last quoted at 91.45, for an underlying money market rate of 8.55%, compared to 91.55 to yield 8.45% last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  It has traded between 91.30 and 91.70 (8.70% and 8.30%) on a hefty volume of 1,186 lots against late Thursday's volume of 820 lots. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 03-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0940GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4302ue2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
