\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Stable Late; Premiums Continue To Move Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 1998\par 12:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar remained steady Thursday but forward premiums continued to climb on nervousness about the weakening regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  Around 0915 GMT (4:15 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7496 against the U.S. dollar, down from HK$7.7495 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar traded in a range of HK$7.7480 and HK$7.7496 so far Thursday and was close to the key support level of HK$7.750. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of speculation nor any indication of imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the much talked about 'April Roll' effect have put dealers on guard. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers reckoned that speculators who bought three-month or six-month positions in January and October would have to decide whether to roll over their positions in April. \par \par \uc2  UBS trader Mitchell Lim said: 'We believe that most banks are not taking any precaution whatsoever against the `April roll' or the thin market between the Ching Ming (Monday) and Easter holidays.' \par \par \uc2  As regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened in the last few days, banks have been scrambling to buy forward contracts to cover their risks, which sent the forward premiums up. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, the one-month premium is quoted at 60 points from 40 points late in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The three-month premium is quoted at 300 points, compared with 250 points previously. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium is quoted at 850 points, down from 780 previously. \par \par \uc2  The one-year premium is quoted at 2500 points, up from 2300 from Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers dismissed the 'April Roll' theory, saying that such speculators should have cut their losses and exited the market. \par \par \uc2  'They would have lost a hefty sum already if they are still holding those positions,' a dealer at an Australian bank said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 4.25%, unchanged from late Wednesday. The three-month rate is 6.625%, down from 6.75% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page\par    -By Noel Fung;(852) 2802 7002;noel.fung@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-04-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1027GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4202tit\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
