\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Flat Late Amid Speculation For Local Rate Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 10:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is flat in dull trading late Wednesday, with investors sidelined amid growing speculation for a local interest rate cut, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  'The regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets have been pretty stable today (Wednesday), and there're no incentives for dealers to take on any new positions right now. People are hoping for a rate cut' in Hong Kong, following a steady decline in interbank rates and a recent rate reduction in Singapore, said a dealer with an European bank. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers say local rates could come down as early as this this week when the Hong Kong Association of Banks, a rate-setting cartel, holds its weekly meeting late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a tight range of HK$7.7473 and HK$7.7485 so far Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0910 GMT (4:10 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7478 per dollar, virtually unchanged from HK$7.7479 late Tuesday, but firmer than HK$7.7485 early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a touch weaker in early trading Wednesday, as investors moved into U.S. dollar positions to benefit from higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The dealer at the European bank said talk of an imminent rate cut is likely to continue to put pressure on the Hong Kong dollar for the rest of the week. 'It will test the HK$7.750 level again' if the banks lower interest rate as expected, he predicted. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, is widely expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the U.S. dollar's rise at HK$7.750, the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month rate is at a five-point discount to the spot rate from a 20-point discount late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month premium edged up to 130 points from 90 points, the six-month premium to 650 points from 540 points, and the one-year premium stood at 2100 points, slightly up from 1800 points late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Patty Zhao; 852 2802 7002; pzhao@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 25-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0925GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3p02jwr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
