\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Early Under Pressure From Falling Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 04:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is slightly lower in early trade, but is under pressure from falling interbank rates and close to a key support level, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0230 GMT (9:30 p.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7486 against the U.S. dollar, slightly lower than HK$7.7488 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a narrow range of HK$7.7485 and HK$7.7488 so far Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they're waiting to see if the Hong Kong dollar spot rate pushes close to HK$7.7500, believed to be an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  point for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The HKMA declined to comment on whether it's an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  point. \par \par \uc2  They said the HKMA was in a difficult position - trying to bring down interbank rates to pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis levels without eroding the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  'Traders are asking, `will the HKMA be there' (at HK$7.75)?' said one dealer with a local bank. 'What can it do? It's trying to bring (interbank) rates down while protecting the Hong Kong dollar.' \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 4.00%, compared with 4.125% late during the previous session. The three-month rate is 6.375%, down from 6.50% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page \par \par \uc2  The falling interbank rates are helping bring forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums down further. \par \par \uc2  The one-month premium is at two points, down from five points late Thursday. The three-month premium is at 120 points, down from 180 points previously. The six-month premium is at 630 points, down from 790 points, and the one-year premium is at 2000 points, down from 2400 points. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0344GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3k02ebu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
