\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weakens, Edging Closer To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Level \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 10:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was weaker late Thursday on steady low interbank market rates. \par \par \uc2  Dealers cited more buying activities on the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Around 0845 GMT (3:45 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7488 against the U.S. dollar, weaker than HK$7.7478 late Wednesday. The Hong Kong dollar traded in a range of HK$7.7472 and HK$7.7488 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar rate is edging slowly closer to the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , generally believed to be HK$7.7500. 'So there is no incentive to trade the spot market because Hong Kong dollar can't get any weaker,' a dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  While the spot market trading is thin, there's more activity in the forward market. Dealers said the low premiums have attracted some buyers. \par \par \uc2  'It is better to buy in the forward market so as to profit from any likely increases in forward premiums,' a dealer at a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  The one-month premium has now been sitting below 10 points for most of the week, after ending January at 106 points, while the three-month premium is under 200 points, after closing January at 1339 points. \par \par \uc2  The one-month premium is at nine points, up from five points late Wednesday. The three-month premium is at 180 points, unchanged. The six-month premium is at 790 points, up from 780 points, and the one-year is unchanged at 2400 points. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 4.125%, unchanged from Wednesday, while the three-month rate is at 6.5%, also unchanged. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page 1085]. \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; (852) 2802 7002; nfung@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0934GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917du3j02gqk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
