\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Down Midday On Falling Rates, Indonesia Worries \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 1998\par 04:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is continuing its move to weaker levels Thursday as interbank rates remain soft and investors display renewed concerns about Indonesia's political and financial situation. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar, also locally called the 'TT,' has pushed up above HK$7.7450 and is quoted at HK$7.7453 at 0335 GMT (10:35 p.m. EST, Wednesday). It was quoted at HK$7.7435 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'As interest rates have moved lower, driving the 'TT' up a little bit, and there is still concern on the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There's the question of whether Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  can recover from this crisis,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said arbitrage opportunities have all but disappeared as interbank rates have fallen this week, meaning the Hong Kong dollar has lost its luster. \par \par \uc2  Concerns that Indonesia will lose its International Monetary Fund bailout package if it proceeds with plans to introduce a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board have also sparked a move into the U.S. dollar, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums, usually the first signal of investor jitters in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are nearly flat. They typically shoot up as investors rush to hedge local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure. The one-month premium is quoted at 70 points, compared with 60 points late Wednesday, the three-month at 470 points from 480 points and the six-month at 1350 points from 1400 points. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the U.S. dollar could test highs of HK$7.7480 later Thursday, but that investors will ease off as the dollar approaches HK$7.7500 on the belief that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam Najberg; 852-2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-02-98 \par \par \uc2  0353GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2j01ihd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
