\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Higher Late; Investors Relax As Asia Mkts Calm \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1998\par 10:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Quiet markets in the rest of Asia are having a calming effect on the Hong Kong dollar, which has moved higher late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is trading at HK$7.7375 at 1000 GMT (5:00 a.m. EST), down from HK$7.393 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Last week, investors tried to push the U.S. dollar below HK$7.7350 without success. On Monday and again on Tuesday morning, they tried to move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the opposite direction. \par \par \uc2  But after the U.S. dollar failed to break above HK$7.7410 Tuesday morning on aggressive buying by European banks, investors took profits, dropping the U.S. dollar down to its current level. \par \par \uc2  The head of money markets at a U.S. bank said investors don't believe the U.S. dollar can break above HK$7.7500 without risking \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As a result, they're not pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much above HK$7.7400. \par \par \uc2  'When it stays at HK$7.7350-7.7400, it's a very comfortable level,' the money markets chief said. \par \par \uc2  The money markets chief said investors in the Hong Kong market aren't motivated to move much, with the rest of the region's markets fairly subdued. Investors have either locked in long U.S. dollar positions for safety's sake, or Hong Kong dollar positions for rate arbitrage. \par \par \uc2  Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums continue to fall, with the one-month premium dropping to 70 points from 90 points late Monday, the three-month to 520 points from 640 points and the six-month premium to 1,450 points from 1,700 points. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; 852-2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-02-98 \par \par \uc2  0952GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2a013p4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
