\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKETS - HK dollar must sink or swim. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mike Dolan \par \uc2 807 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong authorities must either stick with their existing U.S. dollar peg or float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  freely because there is no half way house, foreign analysts said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The existence of such an alternative is probably illusory despite some speculation to the contrary this week, they said. \par \par \uc2  Traders in London said there was talk on Monday that the Hong Kong administration was privately mulling alternatives to its existing fixed exchange rate system, one that would not involve allowing markets complete freedom to set the rate. \par \par \uc2  But a one-step devaluation and refixing or the adoption of a managed depreciation, like the so-called crawling peg, would be unworkable, they said. A watering down of the strict \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, on the other hand, by means of capping market interest rates would only risk undermining confidence further. \par \par \uc2  If the existing peg was forced to go, the only practical option is to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  find its own level, even if this meant an overshoot. Most economists, however, are betting this route will be avoided - at least until there is some substantial correction to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Hong Kong's beleaguered neighbours. \par \par \uc2  "In some respects the Hong Kong peg is working brilliantly and is doing exactly what it is supposed to do. The problem is it's very painful," said Peter Von Maydell, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at UBS in London. Devaluation and deflation are direct substitutes." \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Hang Seng index of leading stocks fell 8.70 percent on Monday as interest rates rose amid fresh speculation about the durability of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fixed exchange rate peg just above 7.7 per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The peg has been in place since 1984 but the Hang Seng has lost more than half its value since August. \par \par \uc2  The relentless \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turbulence across Asia in the second half of 1997 damaged sentiment in Hong Kong too as a analysts reckon the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become anywhere between 10 percent and 40 percent overvalued because of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  collapses elsewhere in the region. \par \par \uc2  Abandoning the existing peg for some other form of managed system would be hard to operate, however. \par \par \uc2  "If they were to devalue and refix the rate lower there would be an automatic assumption that the peg would be broken again. Either interest rates would soar to reflect that lack of confidence or a float would be forced eventually," said Von Maydell at UBS. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs hinge on local and international confidence in their rigidity. Tamper with that in the slightest, analysts argue, and capital will stampede to the exit and cause an overshoot that is impossible to manage in the short-term. \par \par \uc2  "If you convince people that the peg is unassailable and then you alter the rate or the system, it is very hard to do anything except float," said Paul MacNamara, emerging markets economist at Julius Baer Investments. \par \par \uc2  The net result over time, however, of either adjusting the peg or floating is also higher local interest rates because the risk premium required to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would rise. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the authorities are prepared to stick with the devil they know for now in the hope markets will calm further and that the HK dollar will regain some lost competitiveness as the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebound in time. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the growing worry amongst officials in Hong Kong about the impact on the stock market of high interest rates will continue to gnaw away at international and domestic confidence that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board is absolutely rigid. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system set up 14 years ago is aimed at guaranteeing the base money supply at a fixed rate by matching notes and coins one-for-one with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. As a result, market interest rates automatically rise when there is speculation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the system has been diluted in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interest rate markets to prevent excessive rate rises hurting the stock market too much and ultimately damaging the banking system. \par \par \uc2  "There's been a lot of confusion in the market about what exactly the HKMA (Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is doing," said Carlos Daurignac, emerging markets strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  "If it sticks by its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board, then it should allow interest rates to adjust automatically. But by not doing this, it is watering down the whole system," said Daurignac. \par \par \uc2  "This undermines confidence in the willingness to maintain the whole system and to ultimately suffer the pain of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board," he said. "As a result, the urge to hedge will continue." \par \par \uc2  ((Mike Dolan, London newsroom +44 171 542 6762, fax 583 7239, uk.emergingmarkets.news@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1d07wcj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
