\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weaker Early -2: HKMA Says It Was Passive Wed \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par 04:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  News reports in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  have claimed that the HKMA was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in London. \par \par \uc2  But an HKMA source said the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 'passive' Wednesday, merely supplying the Hong Kong dollars necessary for short position holders to exit markets. \par \par \uc2  There were rumors in the afternoon that there might be another bout of speculation against the Hong Kong dollar, the HKMA source said. \par \par \uc2  The source explained that interbank rates climbed because bankers were reluctant to lend for fear that a sudden spike would leave them unable to cover their positions. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates are rising again Thursday. For more interbank-related news, see Dow Jones page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, where heavy hedging activity and speculation were believed to have been going on Wednesday, premiums have begun to steady. \par \par \uc2  That indicates that hedging of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure and speculative short-selling of the Hong Kong dollar have diminished. The result is a slightly less bearish outlook for the Hong Kong dollar than in previous days. \par \par \uc2  The three-month premium is quoted at 1,450 points, compared with 1,500 points late Wednesday. The six-month premium is at 3,300, up a touch from 3,100 points. But participants said it will fall later Thursday. \par \par \uc2  For the spot market, dealers said they expect a U.S. dollar trading range of HK$7.7400-80 for the rest of Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; (852) 2802 7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0351GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du180053o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
