\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steadying In London, NY After Sudden Spike \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par 17:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar has steadied at stronger levels in the London and New York centers Wednesday after spiking to intraday highs near the end of active trading in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar, also referred to as the 'TT,' is quoted at HK$7.7355 at around 1600 GMT, down sharply from HK$7.7500 late Tuesday and the HK$7.7495-98 level at which it traded for most of Wednesday in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Late night television news reports in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  claimed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the London and New York markets to support the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  But a 'TT' dealer at a London-based bank said he has seen no sign of Hong Kong's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in either trading center. \par \par \uc2  He said the Hong Kong dollar actually spiked just after 0900 GMT, with the U.S. dollar briefly touching a low of HK$7.7300 on what market participants believe was one large U.S. dollar sell order that was well-timed to move the market. At 0900 GMT, most Hong Kong-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are closing up shop, and active trading in London hasn't quite begun. \par \par \uc2  'Basically, because of the timing, most liquidity had dried up, most Hong Kong banks were done for the day, and the European markets aren't so liquid,' he said. \par \par \uc2  He said he heard the U.S. dollar sell order was for between US$2.0-3.0 billion and came from a U.S. investment bank. \par \par \uc2  'The selling was very heavy,' he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 07-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1646GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du17004ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
