\par\par \b \uc2  HK Early Hibor Sharply Higher on  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1998\par 03:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates rose early Monday on the back of renewed Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, and shrugged off U.S. Federal Reserve chairman's bullish comments on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 4.375% by Commonwealth Bank of Australian up from 4.125% on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month rate is 10.00%, up from 8.875%-9.125% late Friday. The March three-month Hibor futures contract was quoted at 87.65, down from 88.45 late Friday. The quote implies an interest rate of 12.35%, up from 11.55% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were sharply weaker at the open, putting a floor under Hong Kong interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar means local rates rise as the U.S. dollar rises and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region fall. \par \par \uc2  'The short end has moved by about 30 basis points,' said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Hong Kong dollar spot rate is calling the shots. While it remains at its current level, believed to be a potential trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , interest rates will stay firm. \par \par \uc2  They said U.S. dollars were in demand, hurting the Malaysian ringgit, the Indonesian rupiah and the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said major investors are expected to cut their Hong Kong dollar bills and notes holdings from an average HK$20 million to HK$5 million, hurting sentiment further. \par \par \uc2  Early Monday, the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7500, unchanged from Friday. \par \par \uc2  Sean Kennedy; 852-2802-7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0250GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1500297\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
