\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Early/Profit-Taking -2: Forward Premiums Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1997\par 05:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Few market participants are daring enough in current market conditions to push past HK$7.7500, a level that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at, a treasury chief at an Asian bank said. \par \par \uc2  Premiums in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market rose considerably, though market participants said the increase was purely commercial-driven. A rise in premiums indicates investors are increasingly hedging their Hong Kong dollar exposure. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the six-month premium is quoted at 2,100 points from 1,930 points previously. The three-month premium is quoted at 750 points, compared with 660 points late during the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.5% by Chase Manhattan Bank, up from 4.0625%-4.125% late Monday. The benchmark three-month rate is 9.375%-9.5%, little changed from 9.50%-9.625% late Monday. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones Markets, page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  - By Betty W. Liu; (852) 2802-7002; bwliu@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0447GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcu09zul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
