\par\par \b \uc2  HK dlr steady, forwards little changed at close. \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Dec 22 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar was steady on Monday and dollar forwards were rangebound in thin trade, despite Moody's Asia-related downgrades. \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service announced on Monday that it had downgraded the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  country ceiling for bonds and bank deposits of Indonesia, South Korea, Thailand, Malaysia. \par \par \uc2  It confirmed the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceiling for bonds and bank deposits of Japan, Hong Kong, China, Singapore, Taiwan, Philippines and Vietnam. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume in the local money market was thinner than Friday because most participants had squared positions last week. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said Moody's move may signal that the end of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis was not in sight and a further dive in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to trigger a major sell-off on the local unit as dealers build up new positions when the new year starts. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was at HK$7.7485/7.7505 from Friday's 7.7492/7.7502 close. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  or money market on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The three-month dollar forward was steady from early trade to close at 580-610 points versus 580-620 at Friday's close. The six-month was little changed at 1,750-1,820 points from early trade and 1,775-1,825 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Local interest rates were steady or eased. \par \par \uc2  The three-month Hong Kong dollar deposit rates was indicated at 8.25-9.25 percent versus 9.00-9.12 percent at Friday's close. The six-month was at 9.75-10.75 percent versus 10.25-10.5 percent at Friday's close. -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcm00u50\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
