\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Late Flat; Shrugs Off S. Korea Mkts, HK Stk Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 1997\par 10:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was flat in extremely thin market conditions late Friday, unaffected by both the outcome in South Korea's presidential elections and the steep drop in the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  Traders are reluctant to take on positions so close to the end of the year. Moreover, belief that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would almost certainly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it fell below the HK$7.7500 to the U.S. dollar level is damping activity, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0905 GMT (4:05 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is unchanged at HK$7.7496, compared with late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'Banks and corporates tend to reduce their risks before the holiday,' a chief money markets trader at a European bank said. 'Activity is quite low.' \par \par \uc2  Local traders said the lack of interest in the market allowed investors to shrug off the impact of South Korea's presidential election results, which delivered victory for Kim Dae-jung. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's financial markets fell sharply in response to Kim's victory as fears arose the new leader might not follow through on the tough measures imposed by the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  The sharp fall in the local stock market also failed to rattle the Hong Kong dollar. The blue-chip Hang Seng Index dropped 348.30 points, or 3.2%, to 10,405.81 points on the back of steep losses in the Tokyo and New York markets. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday, the benchmark three-month interbank rate fell below 10%. It is quoted at 9.00%, steady from late Thursday. The usually more volatile overnight rate is steady at 4.0625%. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page \par \par \uc2  -By Betty W. Liu; (852) 2802-7002; bwliu@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0919GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcj09s6i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
