\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Late Up; Boosted By Concerns Of HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par 10:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-Dow Jones)--Easing volatility in the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and concerns the local \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar late Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar's rise, though, was slight since the buying interest came more from fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  than change in sentiment about the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0850 GMT (3:50 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7494, down from HK$7.7497 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'The TT (U.S. dollar against Hong Kong dollar) has been pretty quiet today,' a trader at a European bank said. 'Nobody wants to push it past HK$7.7500 because they're afraid' that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step into the market. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA is rumored to have been in the market selling U.S. dollars each time the U.S. dollar hit HK$7.7500 this week. As a rule, the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on market activities. \par \par \uc2  Though the South Korean won closed lower Wednesday, market participants said calmer market conditions there lifted sentiment in Hong Kong, encouraging banks to lend more. This pushed interest rates lower. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the benchmark three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 8.875%-9.00%, down from late Tuesday's 9.375%. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate is at 4.0%, steady from 4.0%-4.0625% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones Markets, page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0903GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtch09oqu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
