\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor: Rates Lower After Float Of S. Korean Won \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1997\par 10:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates are slightly lower in quiet trading late Tuesday, with investors displaying more calm after a strong debut by the newly floated South Korean won. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended higher by 10% at 1,425 won to the U.S. dollar on the first trading day after the government's late Monday announcement the won would float freely. The news had a soothing effect on market participants about further financial turmoil in the region, making banks in Hong Kong more willing to lend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 9.375%, down from 9.688% late Monday and unchanged from early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight rate is quoted at 4.0%-4.0625%, flat from late Monday and at about the same level as early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a local bank said interbank rates are usually lower when \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading quiets, which it did Tuesday. He said some big domestic banks have been seen lending aggressively Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  He added that rates are relatively steady as the Hong Kong dollar holds at just under HK$7.7500 per U.S. dollar. He suspects the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling further. \par \par \uc2  'We saw positions from Hongkong Bank. It is said that they were positions of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' he said, noting that the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually carries out money market activities through the Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corp., the territory's biggest bank. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA doesn't typically comment on its day-to-day activities in Hong Kong markets. \par \par \uc2  At 0940 GMT (4:40 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7497, unchanged from late Monday and nearly steady from earlier Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  March 1998 Hibor futures are quoted at 88.25, up from late Monday's 87.90, but down from early Tuesday's 88.40. The latest futures quote implies an interest rate of 11.75%, down from 12.10% late Monday, but up from 11.6% Tuesday morning. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0954GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcg09my1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
