\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Late Flat; Key Support At HK$7.7500/U.S. Dlr Level \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1997\par 09:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is flat late Tuesday, with many traders reluctant to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further since it could draw the monetary authorities out into the market. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar spent most of Tuesday hovering near the key HK$7.7500 per U.S. dollar level that many traders said if hit, will immediately prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0831 GMT (3:31 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is unchanged at HK$7.7497 compared with late Monday. \par \par \uc2  'There's quite a bit of offering interest at the HK$7.7498-99 (per U.S. dollar) level...and there's very little interest to take (the U.S. dollar) any higher,' a dealer at an Asian bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the HKMA has already been seen in the market in the past few days when the U.S. dollar peaked at HK$7.7500. As a general rule, the HKMA doesn't comment on its activities. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the recent rise of the Korean won, which is helping restore investor confidence, has also kept the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling through the key support level. \par \par \uc2  Though the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is well-supported, many traders said there is still a huge appetite for U.S. dollars as corporates square up their books before the year closes. \par \par \uc2  'The whole region seems to be in need of U.S. dollars as the end of the year approaches' as many are trying to make payments on their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans, the Asian bank trader said. 'Hong Kong also needs to cover its shortage of U.S. dollars.' \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 9.375%, down from 9.688% late Monday and unchanged from early Tuesday. The overnight rate is at 4.0%-4.0625%, flat from late Monday and about the same level of 4.0313% early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones Markets, page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  -Betty W. Liu; (852) 2802-7002; bwliu@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0845GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcg09mmu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
