\par\par \b \uc2  HK dlr modestly weaker, forwards ease at close. \b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Dec 15 (Reuters) - Despite renewed fears over ailing regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Hong Kong dollar was only modestly weaker on Monday and managed to maintain its key support at HK$7.75, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar ended at HK$7.7495/05 versus 7.7490/HK$7.7510 in early trade and at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Local money market traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) was not seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot or forward market on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rumours that the HKMA might not defend the local unit even if it fell below 7.75 prompted speculators to re-test the Hong Kong dollar peg. \par \par \uc2  "But it seems that they (HKMA) has done something, given the fact it (the HK dollar) has been hovering in such a tight range around 7.75 these two days and still failed to breach that level," a senior dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Market participants believed that the Hong Kong dollar would swiftly dip to HK$7.8 if the defence at HK$7.75 broke, a senior dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers said a lack of genuine trading interest in the Hong Kong dollar spot market towards the year's end helped to ease downward pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Most activity is still on the forward market," a senior dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Further weakening of the Indonesian rupiah in late trade sent US/HK dollar forward off its earlier low, but forward rates still ended softer than Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  The three-month dollar forward was firmer to 790-840 points from 750-850 in early trade but lower than Friday's close of 950-1,050. \par \par \uc2  The six-month rose to 2,150-2,250 points from 1,800-2,000 in early trade but eased slightly from 2,300-2,500 points at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  The three-month Hong Kong dollar deposit rate was slightly higher at 9.12-10.12 percent from 9.0-10 percent in early trade but lower than Friday's close of 10.7-11 percent. The six-month was unchanged at 10.5-11.5 percent versus early trade but slightly lower from Friday's close of 11-12.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  Rating agency Standard and Poor's said on Monday that "if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HK dollar) continues to be tested, interest rates could climb again." \par \par \uc2  S&P said high levels of profitability and capital put Hong Kong banks in a good position to absorb any losses. \par \par \uc2  --Angi LI HK Newsroom 852-2847-4043; Fax 852-2845-0636 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcf0110e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
