\par\par \b \uc2  HK dlr slips through 7.75,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  rumoured. \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 12 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar traded at the key HK$7.75 per U.S. dollar support level on Friday afternoon after repeatedly brushing against it over the past few days, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were rumours the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars for U.S. dollars, but this could not be confirmed. \par \par \uc2  An HKMA spokesman declined to comment on the rumours. \par \par \uc2  The HK$7.75 level is thought by dealers to be closely watched by the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar hovered in an extremely narrow range of HK$7.7490 to HK$7.7495 on Thursday after opening weaker at HK$7.7470/80 versus HK$7.7450/60 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were only a couple of small transactions at the 7.75 level and that there was no major break of support. \par \par \uc2  The bid and ask spread for the Hong Kong and the U.S. dollar was normal at between five and 10 basis points, they said. \par \par \uc2  The forward market looked less nervous, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The three-month dollar forward eased slightly to 900-1,200 points from the 1,050-1,150 quoted at midday and 1,150-1,250 in early trade. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcc0179c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
