\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Sharply Lower Late As  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Concerns Mount \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1997\par 10:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar weakened sharply in volatile trading as nervousness over the spillover effects from the South Korean financial crisis heightened among local traders late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The jitters forced domestic interest rates higher, caused the stock market to plunge and drove the U.S. dollar up near the key HK$7.7500 level. \par \par \uc2  Around 0905 GMT (4:05 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7484, up significantly from HK$7.7440 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'People saw the Korean won dropping further this morning so there was panic-buying of the U.S. dollar,' a money markets chief at a U.S. bank said. 'But (the U.S. dollar) stayed below HK$7.7500 because at that level, the (\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would be there' to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won ended at its daily limit low for the fourth consecutive day, ending late Thursday at 1,719.80 won per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it's hard to discern whether speculative positions are actually building up against the Hong Kong dollar, but many investors are 'cautiously' buying up the U.S. dollar on fears such an attack may occur. \par \par \uc2  As nervousness increases in Hong Kong's markets, domestic banks are borrowing more local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 'protect' their three- and six-month deposits, which is driving interbank rates higher, the money markets chief said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.125%, compared with 4.25% late during the previous session. However, the three-month rate is 11.00%, up from 10.00% late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0922GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcb09hvb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
