\par\par \b \uc2  HK dlr fails to break 7.75 at close, forwards rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Dec 11 (Reuters) -  The Hong Kong dollar ended modestly weaker on Thursday, but failed to convincingly breach key support at HK$7.75 per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The HK$7.75 level is widely regarded as a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  point for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The HK$7.75 is very strong psychological support level," Leo Leung, Treasurer at Bayerische Landesbank said. \par \par \uc2  Strong profit-taking interest on the greenback was seen as the local unit got closer to 7.75 amid fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity by the HKMA, a dealer noted. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was steady at HK$7.7470/80 in late trade versus the open but was still weaker than Wednesday's close of HK$7.7450/60 per U.S dollar. \par \par \uc2  Leung said it would be hard for the Hong Kong dollar not to fall when the Korean won plunged by over 20 percent in three days. The local unit has dropped by 0.15 percent since Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not spotted in either the spot or forward market, though they said they heard the HKMA twice offered three-month money at about 11-11.15 percent into the interbank system in early trade and some shorter-dated money in late trade. \par \par \uc2  The de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained stable and it had no immediate plans to adjust rates at its discount window. \par \par \uc2  Frederic Laine, head of interest rate and derivative trading at Credit Lyonnais in Hong Kong, noted that the recent fall in the Hong Kong dollar coincided with the expiration of the December HIBOR futures contract on December 15. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was sporadic, with no major transactions in either the spot or forward market. \par \par \uc2  "Bids were more aggressive on forwards today, especially on the six-month " a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some major U.S investment were heard buying six and one-year dollar forward. \par \par \uc2  The three-month dollar forward jumped to 1,000-1,100 points from 800-1100 points in early trade and 700/750 at Wednesday's close. The six-month rose to 2,400-2,600 points from 2,200-2,500 in early trade and 1,900-2,200 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the transaction size for forward contract ranged between US$8 million and 20 million on Thursday, which was very normal. \par \par \uc2  However, market talk suggested that some major players tended to break down contract size to avoid attention. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcb015fx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
