\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Falls Late;Confidence In Bks Back,HKMA Rumors Abound \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 1997\par 09:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is weaker Wednesday, but has partly recovered in afternoon trading as investor confidence in the local banking sector picks up and on rumors the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been injecting liquidity into money markets. \par \par \uc2  Around 0820 GMT (3:20 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is stronger at HK$7.7305 from HK$7.7295 late Tuesday. But it is weaker from midday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted as high as HK$7.7310 on the back of moderate U.S. dollar buying that took it as high as HK$7.7340 in London and New York sessions overnight. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's money markets were rocked by a mini-run on the International Bank of Asia on Monday and Tuesday. Rates soared as customers withdrew HK$1.5 billion over the two days. They've eased on Wednesday, with the mini-run appearing to be over. For more money markets news, please see Dow Jones Markets page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a local bank said forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums have dropped Wednesday, reflecting lower money market rates and an easing of jitters that led investors to hedge Hong Kong dollar exposure through the forward market in recent days. \par \par \uc2  The three-month premium is at 1,600 points Wednesday, down from 1,800 points late Tuesday. The six-month premium is down to 2,800 points from 3,100 points. Both are flat from midday. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said he also suspects the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in money markets earlier Wednesday by injecting longer-term funds. \par \par \uc2  -By Daisy S.Y. Wong; (852) 2802-7002 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-11-97 \par \par \uc2  0840GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtbc08l87\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
