\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Slightly Stronger Late As Markets Stabilize \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1997\par 09:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is slightly stronger during afternoon dealings Wednesday but hasn't budged much in recent sessions as Hong Kong's markets show increasing signs of stabilization after last week's turmoil in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stock and money markets. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT (3:30 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7305, slightly lower than the HK$7.7325 quoted around the same time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has traded in a narrow range of HK$7.7280 and HK$7.7330 so far Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong stock market rebounded sharply Wednesday and interbank rates continue to decline toward pre-crisis levels, indicating calm is returning to the markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT (3:30 p.m. EST), local banks quoted the overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate at 6.25%, down from 7% Tuesday, while the three-month rate was quoted at 13%, down from 16% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Hang Seng Index climbed 19% to 10,765.30 Wednesday, erasing much of the market's recent loss. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants are now blaming Hong Kong's financial crisis of the past week on the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and as well, attributing the speedy recovery to the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In an effort to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against speculative attack, the HKMA last week sent interbank rates soaring to unprecedented levels - the overnight rate hit 300% at one point last Thursday - which precipitated the stock market's collapse, the head of Treasury at a major \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank said. \par \par \uc2  'The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, which was totally unnecessary,' he said. 'Many banks and companies got burned by the HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It caused a big collapse in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which spread into other global markets,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury chief said the government body is now playing an active role in the money market in an effort to undo the damage it caused by sending signals to the market that it wants to bring interbank rates back down, he said. \par \par \uc2  -By Kirsti Hastings; 852 2802 7002; khastings@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0857GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtat0888s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
