\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Eased Grip On Hong Kong Rates During Tuesday's Turmoil \b0\par\par\uc2  By Damien McElroy \par \uc2  Staff Reporter \par \uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1997\par 14:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased its tight grip on credit conditions in the money markets Tuesday, in an apparent effort to ease pressure on the territory's battered banks. \par \par \uc2  There was little evidence of speculative attack on the Hong Kong dollar during the session, further reducing the need for high interest rates, said traders. \par \par \uc2  Even before stock trading began in the morning, the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen lending money overnight at rates as low as 5.0%. Almost a week ago, the HKMA's strategy to defend the Hong Kong dollar from speculative attack resulted in money market rates shooting to 300%. \par \par \uc2  "The HKMA was more aggressively lending money because of the impact on the stock market of shaken confidence from high rates," said a trader with a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Market participants said the HKMA was signaling Tuesday that it wanted the overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate at 7.00%. Officially, after a weekend rate hike, the HKMA targets the overnight HIBOR at between 4.00% to 7.00%. \par \par \uc2  The authority itself declined to comment on its market activity, but participants said it also offered enough one-week money to drop the one-week HIBOR to 13% from late Monday's level of 20%. \par \par \uc2  "We have observed that the HKMA has been in the market all day offering liquidity to the banking system. It was providing a signal to the market that it wouldn't like to see interbank rates high for a long time," said the head of treasury at a domestic bank. \par \par \uc2  While the rates have since eased, they remain above levels seen before the markets turmoil began last week, and money market players said they aren't convinced the lower levels are here to stay. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng Index, the leading measure of share price movements in Hong Kong, fell 14% on Tuesday to 9059.89. \par \par \uc2  There was less impact from the HKMA's activity at the longer end of the money market, where rates remained in the middle to high-teens. The three-month rate remained at 16% and the one year HIBOR stood at 15%, well above equivalent U.S. dollar interbank rates, though down of the levels seen at the top of the crisis last week. \par \par \uc2  Because rates remained high for longer terms, the Hong Kong dollar was little affected by the HKMA's money market easing, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was higher amid Tuesday's stock selling, even amid apparent direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the HKMA. It was quoted at HK$7.7325 in late trading, from HK$7.7300 around the same time Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. bank trader said that the HKMA was buying Hong Kong dollars, but he didn't know how much it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Other participants said they saw no signs that the authority was directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In fact, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 -based bank's treasurer said that the steadying Hong Kong dollar on Tuesday confirmed to him that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't really come under significant selling pressure last week. He said the HKMA overreacted, endangering asset values in the territory, such as properties and stocks. \par \par \uc2  "Today confirmed my view that the attack on the Hong Kong dollar has been minimal. The HKMA wanted to prove the government has the power and ability to maintain the pegged rate system. They succeeded in crashing the stock market," he said. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1997 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020011006dtas00w5h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
