\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - HK takes more steps to fend off speculators. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mishi Saran \par \uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 1997\par 08:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Oct 25 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  made it more expensive for banks to borrow money on Saturday to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators at bay, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "It's a cautionary measure to fend off speculators," said Edward Chan, head of research at Amsteel Securities. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said it was adjusting the bid rate under the Liquid Adjustment Facility (LAF) to four percent from 4.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Offer rates rose to seven percent from 6.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  "For banks trying to borrow money, the cost would be slightly higher," said Albert Chan, spokesman for the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  "The reason for doing it is higher volatility in overnight interest rates," Chan said. \par \par \uc2  Widening the LAF corridor would also allow the HKMA more flexibility on interest rate decisions. \par \par \uc2  "The market was much more volatile this week in terms of interest rates, so widening the bid and offer spread of the LAF rates will allow a certain flexibility for the HKMA to manoeuvre the interest rates in an indirect way," said Stanley Wong, regional treasurer at Standard Chartered Bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The HKMA effectively declared war on speculators this week, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate markets to make the cost of attacking the Hong Kong dollar very high for hedge funds, many of them reportedly from the United States. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is the last Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegged to the U.S. dollar and the latest regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come under attack. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates rocketed to 300 percent on Thursday at the peak of the crisis then fell to six percent the next day. \par \par \uc2  "If (speculators) short the Hong Kong dollar, they have to borrow money from the system, so if you raise interest rates, you increase the cost on speculators," Amsteel's Chan said. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index plunged more than 10 percent on Thursday as interest rates surged but clawed back nearly seven percent on Friday on as rates eased. \par \par \uc2  The market turmoil is the worst crisis to hit the territory in decades and the first since it reverted to Chinese rule in July. \par \par \uc2  However, while the HKMA seems to have won the latest battle against speculator, it has not yet won the war, analysts have said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Hong Kong dollar rose sharply to 7.5 against the U.S. dollar on Thursday as speculators cut their losses. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pegged to the U.S. dollar at 7.8 in 1983 but is allowed to move in a narrow range around that. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased to 7.7335/55 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said scaring away the banks which finance speculators was the HKMA's first step in halting attacks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg. \par \par \uc2  "For repeated borrowing, we don't think banks should come to our discount window. If banks manage their finances properly, they shouldn't need to come to us repeatedly," the HKMA's Chan said. \par \par \uc2  Widening the LAF spread would also help maintain Hong Kong dollar interest rates at a higher level, Wong said. \par \par \uc2  "To widen the spread so banks will have to borrow from the HKMA at 75 basis points higher than before will imply that Hong Kong dollar interest rates will be maintained at a higher level for a prolonged period," Wong said. \par \par \uc2  He said Hong Kong dollar interest rates would stay at double digits next week as policy-makers and investors keenly watch for any signs that speculators have abandoned the market. \par \par \uc2  "It's very much a wait-and-see attitude," Wong said. \par \par \uc2  -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6358 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtap03k8d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
