\par\par \b \uc2  Peregrine/HK Dlr Peg -2: Cuts HK Weighting, Warns China \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 1997\par 09:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg officially values the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HK$7.8000. \par \par \uc2  The Peregrine report said the best solution would be to unify the Hong Kong dollar with the Chinese yuan. 'This would clear the air and provide the smoothest way of abandoning the peg. The trouble is that such a policy switch is most unlikely, given the reluctance of China to go towards capital account convertibility, plus the fact that the very continued existence of the Hong Kong dollar symbolizes the `one country, two systems' post-1997 formula,' said the report. \par \par \uc2  But, said Peregrine, Hong Kong may now be confined to suffering 'from a permanent risk premium. If so, stock market investors may soon start to conclude that the best move for the equity market, given recent declines, would be to abandon the peg as quickly as possible.' \par \par \uc2  The report is also critical of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rather than letting overnight interest rates 'reflect the full pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  Peregrine said the HKMA's action suggests the authority is trying to preserve asset values, and 'the trouble with this policy is that it has reminded investors of what happened in Thailand and other places.' \par \par \uc2  Noting Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock market weakness, Peregrine said a hole has been blown in the Greater China story, 'which was the one last positive in the beleaguered region.' \par \par \uc2  'We will adjust our asset allocation in Hong Kong to a neutral weighting and put the funds raised into cash,' said Peregrine. 'We will retain our overweight position in China for now, given its belated monetary easing.' \par \par \uc2  However, Peregrine also warned that Chinese authorities have been 'slow to react to the evidence of deteriorating investors sentiment toward the region.' The turn in sentiment will make it more difficult to do fund raising in Hong Kong, said Peregrine. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0712GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtao081hx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
