\par\par \b \uc2  HK  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Adds HK$1.982 Bln To Money Market \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 1997\par 15:33\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--After comments by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities that they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to\par defend the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , money market activity by the Hong\par Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday resulted in a net addition\par of HK$1.982 billion.\par    In conducting overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with commercial banks\par that approached its discount window, the quasi \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par made a withdrawal of HK$2.082 billion, not including the\par reversal of day-earlier activity at its discount window,\par known as the liquidity adjustment facility (LAF).\par    This activity left the quasi \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with a balance\par Thursday of HK$3.605.0 billion in the money market, up by\par HK$2.921.0 billion from Wednesday.\par    The overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate (Hibor)\par soared to an intraday high of 300%, before settling down to\par 150% in Asian trading, compared with 5.00% late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    As the quasi \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the HKMA operates Monday\par through Friday in the Hong Kong dollar money markets between\par about 0130 GMT and 0800 GMT. (It sometimes operates on\par Saturday morning, as well.) The activity helps it ensure the\par territory's U.S. dollar-peg of US$1.00 equal to HK$7.8000 is\par maintained, while also helping to accommodate liquidity\par needs of local banks.\par    Late Thursday, the U.S. dollar was at HK$7.7100, down\par sharply from HK$7.7499 late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS  10-23-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0933EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4292 4300 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtan029e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
