\par\par \b \uc2  HK Govt/Peg Viability -2: Stock Market At 19-Month Low \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 1997\par 13:43\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Basic Law is the cornerstone of China's "one\par country, two systems" policy that ensures the territory will\par remain semi-autonomous under Beijing rule.\par    As a sign of that autonomy, Tsang and HKMA Chief\par Executive Joseph Yam said China hasn't made any offer to\par support the territory's sagging markets or the Hong Kong\par dollar. A Foreign Ministry spokesman in Beijing said the\par central government has no plans to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The peg, which has linked the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar to its\par U.S. counterpart at HK$7.8000 since September 1983, is a key\par symbol of this policy.\par    "I don't think they can afford to question the peg at\par this time. It's just too key to the stability in Hong Kong.\par What they're going to do is bear it," said Henry Lee,\par investment director at the Hendale Asia Fund in Hong Kong.\par    The Hang Seng Index plunged 1211.47 points, or 10%,\par Thursday to a 19-month low of 10,426.30 points.\par    The Hong Kong dollar finished stronger compared with\par closing levels Wednesday due to U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar selling by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , ending Asian trading at HK$7.6965 per\par US$1.00 from HK$7.7499 a day ago.\par    The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded in an unusually wide band of\par HK$7.4850 and HK$7.7500 to the U.S. dollar, which is outside\par the 1% trading band believed to be allowed by the HKMA.\par    In the government bond market, yields soared to\par unprecedented highs, with the one-week Exchange Fund bill\par hitting 39%, rising as the interbank Hong Kong Interbank\par Offered Rate surged to 300%.\par    Interest rate and forward market premium levels began to\par change so rapidly after the HKMA announced Liquidity\par Adjustment Facility borrowing restriction at 0130 GMT that\par moneybrokers, such as Exco, chose to wipe out their\par electronic price quote screens for the rest of the trading\par session. Bond dealers said bid-offer spreads were too\par impossibly wide to make any trade feasible.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  10-23-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0743EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1145 4060 4144 4205 62559 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtan029ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
