\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Up Late; Banks Cover Short Positions As Rates Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1997\par 10:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Banks are scrambling to cover short positions as money market rates fall, moving the Hong Kong dollar stronger late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading between HK$7.7420-30 Wednesday morning but dropped in the afternoon to a low of HK$7.7389. It is quoted at HK$7.7394 at 4:22 a.m. EDT (0822 GMT). \par \par \uc2  With speculation and hedging activity last Friday leading to money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a number of banks were caught short in the interbank and forward markets, said the head of Treasury at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  As part of a move to keep the Hong Kong dollar steady and rid the market of speculators, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sucked liquidity out of money markets, driving rates up to 9.00% across the board, well above its benchmark of 4.25% to 6.25%. \par \par \uc2  Speculation eased on Tuesday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to have injected liquidity into money markets, allowing rates to slip closer to the benchmark. Banks that had been caught short had been reluctant to move while rates were high. They're covering, and in some cases, closing out positions Wednesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  'They were very surprised by the very sharp movement, and they're more than a little bit happy to see them (rates) come down,' the Treasury chief said. \par \par \uc2  Demand for the Hong Kong dollar in money markets has also spilled into the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the head of Treasury said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0822GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8k0653q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
