\par\par \b \uc2  HK:Shares Seen Opening Lower On  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Problems, U.K. Drop \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1997\par 03:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong stocks are expected to tumble Tuesday, in the wake of a selloff of Hong Kong shares in London trading, and persistent concerns about the strength of the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong market was closed Monday for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  However, a mild rebound in the New York stock market Monday is expected to lend some support to the beleaguered Hong Kong market. Hong Kong stocks fell sharply Friday, with the Hang Seng index dropping 400.83 points, or 2.4%, to close at 16,096.88 points. \par \par \uc2  'I expect the market will fall (Tuesday), but of course, the rebound on Wall Street will provide some support,' said Ben Kwong, research director at Dharmala Securities Co. Ltd. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 108.70 points to 7803.36 points Monday. \par \par \uc2  Kwong said he expects the Hang Seng index to find support around 15,500 points, with further support seen at 15,300 points. \par \par \uc2  'Of course, the Hong Kong stock market will be affected by the trend in the U.K., but the rebound in the U.S. will offer some support,' he noted. The U.K. market in Hong Kong shares lost a further 525 points to close at 15,571.88 points Friday. Shares were led down by losses in index heavyweight banking stock HSBC Holdings, which fell HK$13.50 to HK$258.50 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Banking and property stocks are expected to be especially weak Tuesday, because of concern about the Hong Kong dollar's recent weakness, and rising Hong Kong dollar bond yields. But the fact that interest rates in the U.S. appear mostly stable is a positive factor, said Kwong. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market participants said Tuesday they are expecting a volatile week of trading in the Hong Kong dollar, following speculative attempts and talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES ASIAN EQUITIES REPORT  19-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0137GMT \par \par \uc2  5013 55108 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011004dt8j012qf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
