\par\par \b \uc2  HK$ Market Stabilizes; Stocks, Bonds Hit Hard-Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1997\par 12:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was stabilizing by the end of Tuesday, but only after local stocks and bonds got hit hard on concerns that the Hong Kong dollar has become the region's latest target for speculators. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hovered around HK$7.7435 for most of Tuesday in thin, but tense, trading that most probably culminated with direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But speculative pressure on the spot and forward Hong Kong dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates wasn't so strong as on Friday, said participants. And there is still little concern that Hong Kong faces a true challenge of its U.S. dollar peg, the last remaining formal link for a major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia that values US$1 at HK$7.8000. \par \par \uc2  Hang Seng Bank Ltd. treasurer Rita Chan said she wouldn't yet declare an end to the bout of speculation, but noted that last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Tuesday's thin trading are a sign that speculators have at least temporarily paused to consider their positions. \par \par \uc2  'People are definitely taking a `wait-and-see' attitude,' she said. 'We definitely see the HKMA has the upper hand.' \par \par \uc2  Just before 0800 GMT, late in the Hong Kong day but at the beginning of European trade, the U.S. dollar strengthened to HK$7.7385. That is one of the weaker levels seen since about late May against the Hong Kong dollar, and compares with levels around HK$7.7500 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA is believed to have made a pre-emptive strike against would-be speculators, two market participants said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1030GMT \par \par \uc2  1134 4204 55128 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8j064fp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
