\par\par \b \uc2  Mkts Brace For More HK$ Speculation,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1997\par 03:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market participants said early Tuesday they're bracing themselves for a volatile week of trading in the Hong Kong dollar, following speculative inroads made last week. \par \par \uc2  After market talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a three-day trading layoff, the Hong Kong dollar is at unusually strong levels early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But participants said they don't expect it to stay there, and that the U.S. dollar could rise as far as HK$7.7500. Around that point, one participant said, the HKMA could be expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is trading at HK$7.7405 at 0110 GMT (9:10 p.m. EDT Monday), down from HK$7.7495, the level at which it traded for most of Friday. \par \par \uc2  Despite the expected pressure, no one is predicting an imminent end to the peg, which values US$1.00 at HK$7.8000 and is the only major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg left in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong government and the quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent the long weekend talking tough through the local press and claiming Hong Kong dollar speculators have been squeezed out of the market. \par \par \uc2  But market participants said Tuesday the tough talk is being interpreted in the market as a sign of nervousness from the government. \par \par \uc2  Aggravating the situation is the U.S. dollar's rise against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the region Monday and weakness for Hong Kong stocks traded overseas, said the head of treasury at an Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  'It is sure that the market will be very volatile in the next few days. The main reason is the other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday depreciated a lot. This will have a very negative effect on the Hong Kong dollar, even though the government said it did stamp out speculators,' the treasury chief said. \par \par \uc2  'It's very likely the market will be speculated again today and in the next few days,' he added. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0110GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8j062ox\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
