\par\par \b \uc2  HK Shrs End Sharply Down On  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Worries, Profit-Taking \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par 10:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Hong Kong stocks ended down as it plunged on a late afternoon sell-off, prompted by worries about the stability of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and profit-taking before a long weekend. \par \par \uc2  The blue-chip Hang Seng Index ended significantly lower Friday, losing 400.83 points, or 2.4%, to close at 16,096.88. It tested a low of 16,002.90 and a high of 16,555.51 during Friday's session. \par \par \uc2  'The Hong Kong dollar exchange rate isn't that stable, and people are taking profits before the long weekend,' said a trader at Yamaichi International (Hong Kong) Ltd. The Hong Kong stock exchange will be closed Monday because of a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar's overnight interbank lending rates shot up to 7% early Friday, but the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only marginally weaker Friday, suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to support the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Equity traders said Friday's market decline was led by interest rate-sensitive banking and property sectors, as investors were worried about a hike in the prime interest rates, driven up by higher money market rates. \par \par \uc2  The broader All Ordinaries Index was down 165.28 points at 8254.38. \par \par \uc2  Turnover was HK$30.72 billion, compared with HK$29.11 billion in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0817GMT \par \pa