\par\par \b \uc2  HK: Shares Drop Mid-morning Affected By HK Dollar Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par 05:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--A spike in Hong Kong interbank lending rates early Friday has hit share prices pulling the main Hang Seng Index about 0.5% lower. \par \par \uc2  At 0311 GMT (11:11 p.m. EDT) the Hang Seng Index is down 81.88 points at 16415.83 points, recovering from its session low at 16346.75. The index traded as high as 16555.51 points at one point. \par \par \uc2  'The pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cause interest rates to move up. People are wondering if turmoil in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues whether the prime interest rate will have to go up,' said Percy Au-yeung research director of DBS Securities Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Money market rates have climbed to levels around 7.00% and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is only marginally weaker Friday, suggesting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Alvin Chan, a trader with MeesPierson Securities Asia Ltd. said ahead of a holiday on Monday investors didn't want to be exposed to market gyrations during the break. \par \par \uc2  'This is the last trading day before the long weekend. Everywhere else is open while Hong Kong is closed, people tend to be conservative,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The trader added that futures contract also indicate participants are bearish. The Hang Seng August future is quoted at 16,305 points. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the U.S. dollar is only a touch higher than Thursday's HK$7.7480 in Asia at HK$7.7490 as of 0325 GMT (11:25 p.m. EDT.)