\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 /Peg System -4: Many Lines Of Defense \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1997\par 08:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'He used this as an illustration that, no, it's not entirely true. The Hong Kong dollar could be (opened) up to speculation,' the spokeswoman says. 'All he wanted to say is we acted swiftly.' \par \par \uc2  The spokeswoman declined to comment about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary authorities were adjusting policy, in that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities would now be announced to the market when they take place. She says announcements would be considered on a case-by-case basis. \par \par \uc2  Commonwealth Bank's Fung says that even if the announcement is a one-time event, speculators should take it as a warning. \par \par \uc2  With only a handful of market makers, real-time settlement and most Hong Kong dollar trading onshore, there's virtually no way to acquire a sizable-enough short position to mount a serious challenge to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and little chance that such a buildup would escape the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's attention. \par \par \uc2  Fung said that to establish the equivalent of a US$5.0 billion to US$8.0 billion position in Hong Kong, a speculator would have to short HK$40.0 billion in forwards. \par \par \uc2  'You can't short HK$40.0 billion in Hong Kong,' Fung said. 'Your counterparty is limited in forwards. Even if you wanted to go short, what kind of funds could you raise?' \par \par \uc2  And even if speculators could force the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to deplete its massive reserves, they would next have to face the People's Bank of China and its more than US$121.20 billion of reserves, a portion of which it has pledged to use in defense of the Hong Kong dollar, if asked. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0636GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 0918GMT) \par \par \uc2  1137 62554 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8d05zma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
