\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Lower Midday As Traders Liquidate Long Positions \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1997\par 05:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Traders began the week Monday liquidating some long Hong Kong dollar positions, driving the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower against its U.S. counterpart in remarkably quiet mid-morning dealings. \par \par \uc2  After scrambling for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars in recent days amid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders reversed their positions and unloaded the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the market early Monday. \par \par \uc2  However, trading is thin owing to fears any huge positions, which could bump the exchange rate around, could draw the wrath of the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  'Positions are being liquidated from Friday which is easing some pressure on the longer-dated forward market rates,' a chief trader at a Hong Kong bank said. 'But everything's pretty stable because nobody wants to challenge the HKMA.' \par \par \uc2  Forward rates eased below 1,000.00 points Monday, indicating that banks are no longer seeking long-term funding to hedge their Hong Kong dollar exposure. \par \par \uc2  The one-year forward contract slid to 930.00 points, down from 1,100.00 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0325 GMT (11:25 p.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7410, up from HK$7.7405 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit is expected to trade in a range of HK$7.7405 to HK$7.7415 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Short-term interbank rates stayed firm, with all but the overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate above 7.00%. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the HKMA is keeping market conditions tight to deter speculation by making the cost of funding painfully expensive. \par \par \uc2  The overnight Hibor is at 6.50% Monday, up from 6.375% late Friday. The one-week rate is flat at 7.00%. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0335GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7s05k71\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
