\par\par \b \uc2  HK$ Bonds Mostly Unchanged But Yields Remain Firm \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1997\par 10:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Hong Kong government bonds were mostly unchanged late Monday, but yields remained firm amid a continuing tight interest rate environment, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said activity calmed down from last week, when volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  caused widespread selling in short-term bonds. \par \par \uc2  The focus Monday, however, returned to U.S. Treasurys which were narrowly mixed before the onslaught of U.S. economic data later in the week. \par \par \uc2  Late Monday, the 10-year Exchange Fund bond yield fell to 6.76%, compared with 6.78% Friday. The one-week Exchange Fund bill yield was flat at 6.30%. \par \par \uc2  Around 0850 GMT (4:50 a.m. EDT), the overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate was quoted at 6.25%, down from 6.375% Friday. The one-week rate was unchanged at 7.00% compared with Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at HK$7.7407, up slightly from HK$7.7405 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  For more information on Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market activity, bill and note prices and other related information, please refer to Dow Jones Markets page \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0859GMT \par \par \uc2  4178 5096 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7s05f52\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
