\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Up On Short-Covering Carried From NY, London \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 1997\par 05:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--A bout of short-covering carried over from the London and New York sessions is driving the Hong Kong dollar slightly higher against its U.S. counterpart midday Friday. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York or London, driving the U.S. dollar below HK$7.7400, prompted traders to cover short positions in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'The U.S. dollar hit a low of HK$7.7365 in London...and whether the HKMA did the selling is not confirmed,' a trader at a European bank said. 'People are taking up short-term money in the market...and trying to cover up all their shorts. It shows the downside to the Hong Kong dollar will be limited.' \par \par \uc2  But 'the turmoil isn't over,' he added. \par \par \uc2  Around 0315 GMT (11:15 p.m. EDT Thursday), the U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7417, down from HK$7.7445 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit has traded in a range of HK$7.7430 and HK$7.7400 so far Friday. \par \par \uc2  High short-term interbank rates - hovering around the 7.00% level - also encouraged selling in the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  'I think the HKMA squeezed rates high enough that it pushed people to sell the U.S. dollar,' another dealer at a Hong Kong bank said. 'That's what's driving the U.S. dollar down compared to yesterday,' he said. \par \par \uc2  In recent days, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been buzzing with talk that speculators are poised to attack the Hong Kong dollar amid the turmoil affecting Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Thursday, traders said the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt markets to stabilize the pegged exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0357GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7p05dj5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
