\par\par \b \uc2  Regional  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Concerns Again Spill Into HK Markets \b0\par\par\uc2  By Adam S. Najberg and Betty W. Liu \par \uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 1997\par 12:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (AP-Dow Jones)--Forward rates moved sharply higher Thursday for the second time this week in what some participants said might mean speculators are poised to attack the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  When the rupiah plunged Monday, banks paid a hefty premium to hedge their Hong Kong dollar exposure. Likewise, pressure on the baht and ringgit Thursday sent banks back into the Hong Kong dollar forward markets. \par \par \uc2  'There's obviously a contagion effect from regional markets,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the U.S. dollar premium rose above Monday's 900.0 points, soaring all the way to 1200.0 points and above Wednesday's 500.0-900.0 premium in Asian trading. The premium has slipped slightly, but remains at 1100.0 points at 1042 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The premium level implies that participants expect a sharply weaker Hong Kong dollar at HK$7.8645 per U.S. dollar a year from now. The U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7441 at 1042 GMT, down from HK$7.7475 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Participants said concern that the Hong Kong dollar spot rate would weaken and that a window would open for speculators prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both the debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The head of money markets at a North American bank said he believes the HKMA sold just under US$100.0 million of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HK$7.7470 to signal it didn't want forward market volatility affecting the spot rate. \par \par \uc2  And a bond trader at a market-making bank said late Thursday that the forward market activity also prompted the HKMA to sell HK$100-200 million of one-month bills at around 0230 GMT to drain liquidity out of the system, drive up money market rates and discourage potential speculation. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman declined to comment on the quasi \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's activities Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1055GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7o05h55\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (hong kong near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\fa